{"tool_name":"isaac","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"isaac","home":"https://github.com/sequencing","summary":"ISAAC comprises of genome aligner and variant caller, by Illumina.","addition_date":"2017-01-13T13:15:08Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:33:55.059433Z","tool_type":["Suite"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:isaac","credit":[{"email":"craczy@illumina.com","name":"ISAAC support","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["Terms of use"],"url":"https://github.com/sequencing/licenses/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3182"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"ISAAC","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"seqwiki_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btt314","metadata":{"abstract":"An ultrafast DNA sequence aligner (Isaac Genome Alignment Software) that takes advantage of high-memory hardware (>48 GB) and variant caller (Isaac Variant Caller) have been developed. We demonstrate that our combined pipeline (Isaac) is four to five times faster than BWA + GATK on equivalent hardware, with comparable accuracy as measured by trio conflict rates and sensitivity. We further show that Isaac is effective in the detection of disease-causing variants and can easily/economically be run on commodity hardware.Availability: Isaac has an open source license and can be obtained at https://github.com/ sequencing.Contact: Supplementary information: Supplementary data are available at Bioinformatics online. \u00a9 2013 The Author 2013. Published by Oxford University Press.","authors":[{"name":"Chorny I."},{"name":"Chuang H.-Y."},{"name":"Kallberg M."},{"name":"Kruglyak S."},{"name":"Kumar S.A."},{"name":"Liao A."},{"name":"Little K.M."},{"name":"Margulies E.H."},{"name":"Petrovski R."},{"name":"Raczy C."},{"name":"Saun